#: index.docbook:56
msgid	"Introduction"
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:58
msgid	"&kab; is an address book for use with &kde; that lets you save "
	"names, postal, email, talk and <acronym>www</acronym> addresses, "
	"telaphone numbers, important dates and other information in a card "
	"index form."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:62
msgid	"&kab; has two basic views, <guimenuitem>Business Card</guimenuitem> "
	"and <guimenuitem>Editing</guimenuitem>. You can switch between them "
	"with the <guimenu>View</guimenu> menu."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:67
msgid	"<guimenuitem>Business Card</guimenuitem> View"
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:69
msgid	"Here's a screenshot of &kab;"
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:69
msgid	"&kab; in card view mode"
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:81
msgid	"This view lets you see what information has been stored for each "
	"entry in &kab;'s database"
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:84
msgid	"To select a particular entry you can pick it from the Drop Down box "
	"in the Toolbar, or you can step through the entries using the "
	"<guiicon>large Toolbar arrows</guiicon> or with your keyboard arrow "
	"keys."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:88
msgid	"You can also search the database for a particular entry by using the "
	"<link "
	"linkend=\"kab-edit-menu\"><menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenu"
	"item>Search entries</guimenuitem></menuchoice></link> option."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:93
msgid	"At the top of the main card area you can see the name as it appears "
	"in the Toolbar Drop Down box list, and possibly an important date "
	"such as the person's Birthday."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:97
msgid	"An address will be shown in the middle of the card. &kab; lets you "
	"enter more than one address, for - say - Home, Work and Holiday "
	"Dacha. The Drop Down box above the address then lets you select "
	"which of these is displayed."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:101
msgid	"The bottom of the card shows email addresses, "
	"<acronym>URL</acronym>s and telephone numbers. Left click on the "
	"email address to send an email, on the <acronym>URL</acronym> to "
	"open a browser window. If you have entered more than one email "
	"address or <acronym>URL</acronym>, then only one will be displayed "
	"on the card followed by [..] and when you click on it a little "
	"dialog box will appear so that you can choose the address you want."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:108
msgid	"The <link linkend=\"kab-file-menu\"><guimenu>File</guimenu> "
	"menu</link> has options allowing you to create and use more than one "
	"database, import your old KDE 1 address book, print one or all "
	"entries, and export the database in <acronym>HTML</acronym> format."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:114
msgid	"<guimenuitem>Editing</guimenuitem> View"
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:116
msgid	"Here's another screenshot of &kab;"
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:116
msgid	"&kab; in edit view mode"
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:128
msgid	"This view is used to add or change the details for a card. It has "
	"four tab pages; <guilabel>Person</guilabel>, "
	"<guilabel>Telephone</guilabel>, <guilabel>Address</guilabel> and "
	"<guilabel>Birthday</guilabel>."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:132
msgid	"The <guilabel>Person</guilabel> tab page is where you enter the "
	"person's name and Email and Talk addresses and any associated "
	"<acronym>URL</acronym>s. Whatever you enter in the "
	"<guilabel>Formatted name:</guilabel> text box will appear as the "
	"entry's name in the Toolbar Drop Down list and at the top left of "
	"the card. If you do not enter anything in the <guilabel>Formatted "
	"name:</guilabel> text tox then &kab; will automatically generate a "
	"formatted name such as <quote>Holmes, Sherlock</quote>."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:140
msgid	"The <guilabel>Telephone</guilabel> tab page is, obviously, where you "
	"enter the telephone number(s)."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:143
msgid	"The <guilabel>Addresses</guilabel> tab page lets you enter one or "
	"more addresses for this entry."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:146
msgid	"For each address you want to enter, click on the "
	"<guibutton>Add</guibutton> button. It will display a drop down list "
	"with one blank entry plus any address types you have set up with the "
	"<menuchoice><guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure this "
	"file...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> option. Choose one and it will "
	"appear in the <guilabel>Headline:</guilabel> text box where you can "
	"edit it if required."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:146
msgid	"Then fill in the address details."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:146
msgid	"Pressing the <guibutton>Insinuation...</guibutton> button brings up "
	"another dialog box where you can enter details of any organisation "
	"that the person works for and his position within it. However, the "
	"current version of &kab; does not display this information in the "
	"<guimenuitem>Business Card</guimenuitem> view."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:162
msgid	"The <guilabel>Birthday</guilabel> tab page is where you select a "
	"significant date to appear at the top right of the card view. It "
	"will only appear if you have checked the <guilabel>I know this "
	"persons birthday:</guilabel> box."
msgstr	""

#: index.docbook:167
msgid	"You will probably need to experiment with your entries in the "
	"<guilabel>Person</guilabel> and <guilabel>Addresses</guilabel> tab "
	"pages to get the kind of result you want in the Card view."
msgstr	""

